questions.requirements:
Prepare a report for the board of directors of McKeever Co which:

(i) Estimates the project’s Erat-based cash flows, in pounds;

(8 marks)

(ii) Estimates the net present value (NPV) of the project in dollars;

(9 marks)

(iii) Evaluates the impact of the marketing director’s alternative exchange rate assumption on the project’s NPV, recommending whether or not the project should be accepted;

(6 marks)

(iv) Discusses the assumptions made in the NPV calculations and responds to the marketing director’s concerns about the methodology used to estimate the expected exchange rates in (ii);

(8 marks)

(v) Discusses the political risks the board should consider before making a final decision;

(5 marks)

(vi) Discusses the validity of the chief executive officer’s suggestion to adjust the project’s discount rate to incorporate country risk.

(4 marks)

Professional marks will be awarded for the demonstration of skill in communication, analysis and evaluation, scepticism and commercial acumen in your answer.

(10 marks)

(a) Explain why countries might impose protectionist measures on imports and the possible economic benefits if Amasia forms a customs union with its neighbouring countries.

(7 marks)

(b) Prepare a report for the board of directors of Mahoney Co which:

(i) Calculates the impact on intra-group cash flows if multilateral netting is used to settle outstanding balances;

(7 marks)

(ii) Calculates the results of using the forward and futures markets to hedge the disposal proceeds from the divestment of Oliviera Co;

(6 marks)

(iii) Briefly discusses, using the results from parts (i) and (ii) above:

• the advantages and disadvantages of the policy to settle intra-group balances;

• whether the forward or futures market would be a better choice to hedge Oliviera Co’s disposal proceeds;

(5 marks)

(iv) Compares the net present value (NPV) in € of the regeneration project in Amasia when either the currency swap or the currency option is used to hedge the project’s cash flows;

(7 marks)

(v) Discusses, using the results from part (iv) above:

• whether the currency swap or currency option would be a better choice to hedge the risk associated with the project in Amasia;

• the assumptions made when estimating the regeneration project’s NPV;

• whether the regeneration project should be undertaken.

(8 marks)

Professional marks will be awarded for the demonstration of skill in communication, analysis and evaluation, scepticism and commercial acumen in your answer.

(10 marks)
